{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/856853-cofd-questions-about-combat-willpower-and-slashers-oh-my","id":856853,"title":"CofD Questions about Combat & Willpower, and Slashers, oh my...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-31T19:12:40-07:00","id":856853,"title":"CofD Questions about Combat & Willpower, and Slashers, oh my...","content":"I'm posting here because I'm not sure exactly where to post this, so please feel free to move this is needs be...<br /> I've been playing White Wolf games for a while now. I started with WoD, rolled with things into nWoD, and now we are getting ready to finally change over to CofD. WoD had the Big Book of Beating Ass, which was amazing and so much fun. nWoD had Armory, Armory Reloaded with Fighting Styles spread throughout other books from time to time.<br /> So here is the rub. My group and I are about to make the big change over to CofD and I know they have questions about fighting style and how things are going to change. I've been reading through the book and so far one of the biggest things Ive noticed is that to have any kind of fight you will have to spend huge (comparatively) amounts of willpower. or am I wrong in that? Are there more ways to regain willpower? because it seemed like in WoD and nWoD using up all your willpower was REALLY bad. not just for mortals but for EVERYONE. Is combat getting nerfed? I kinda feel like it is. I know a lot of things are changing with merits and such, but I'm trying to get as much information as possible before My group starts asking the questions. I know the Hurtlocker is coming up, and I looking forward to it. We even have a slasher in out group (its basically becoming a/is a, cancer cell at this point lol) how does that fit into things? I could use some advice and help on where to find things in the new core book. I would appreciate your help, thank you! Links are welcome if this has all been covered elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11556-coyoteschosen","name":"CoyotesChosen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11556_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-31T19:52:56-07:00","id":856878,"title":"","content":"So first of all, your observation is definitely accurate, spending Willpower in combat is much more important in CofD. Defense values are easier to raise with Athletics being applied to defense now, and attack pools are a little lower because weapons no longer add bonus dice. That said, a successful hit is much more devastating. Weapons add directly to damage on a hit, and all weapons deal lethal damage. Additionally, dealing enough damage in one attack can cause Tilts, which can really screw the target over, especially the Beaten Down Tilt which can straight up end combats. On paper this can look a bit off, especially if you're thinking about it in terms of nWoD 1e combat. It's very common for new players to look a the changes to combat and ask something to the tune of &quot;won't this just be a whiff fest until someone gets a lucky roll, and then it's just over?&quot; but I've found that it works very well if you change your tactics. CofD combat is much less about trying to roll as many dice as possible as fast as possible until someone gets enough 8's 9's and 10's to win. It's much more about manipulating circumstances to your advantage so you can be sure you'll get the hit in when it matters. Focusing fire on single targets becomes important. Targeting specific areas for extra effects on a hit becomes important. Using creative tactics and taking advantage of terrain to score situational dice bonuses becomes important. All-out attacks become important. And yes, spending willpower becomes very important. But if you play it smart, you usually won't have to spend a <i>ton</i> of Willpower.<br /> <br /> As for Willpower recovery, it is a little easier in CofD. For one thing, you don't have to put yourself at risk to regain Willpower from your Vice. Willpower recovery from Virtue is still limited to once per chapter but it can happen at any time during the chapter instead of always coming at the end. There's a Merit that lets you regain Willpower by having a meaningful interaction with a (specific) close friend. Surrendering in combat gives you Willpower back. Lots of supernatural templates have extra ways to regain Willpower. If this is a hunter game, there's always Risking Willpower. And perhaps most importantly, the book advises the storyteller to be generous enough with Willpower so that the players don't feel like they have to horde it. You should make an effort to give characters an opportunity to indulge in their Virtue and Vice frequently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T09:21:28-07:00","id":857165,"title":"","content":"There's also merits that give you an extra virtue and an extra vice, so it is potentially easier to get willpower now. Especially since there's no actual rule that says you can't have both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T17:35:30-07:00","id":858626,"title":"","content":"Thank you both for the answers! That not only helps, but helps sooth My players questions about the game system switch. Are there any good links for converting Slashers merits, and Fighting Styles into the new CofD System that you all maybe able to direct Me to?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11556-coyoteschosen","name":"CoyotesChosen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11556_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T23:42:24-07:00","id":858796,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/15PLeCG-9xqTTaz66JQgLTQHE8OE6-pqsG-6NDddKzok/mobilebasic\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a> is a link to the first draft of non-Fighting Style Merits in Hurt Locker, and <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bH4XMrM7iovLQGBLJGVXHDTGXUrNc0JMy22wc-5MxZ8/mobilebasic\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> is the draft for fighting styles. Keep in mind, these are drafts and will probably look a bit different in the final release, but if you're looking for more combat-related Merits that suit CofD, these will at least be a start.<br /> <br /> If you want an expanded weapons, armor, and equipment list for CofD, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2K8R3qXyDyoWEo5eVNMN0MtUWc/view\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> is a link to the second draft of that Appendix in Hurt Locker. Note that this draft uses an alternative system for range and ammo. Personally, I much prefer this approach to the default, but if you want ranges measured in yards and ammo measured by the bullet, check out the versions from the first draft of the same appendix <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vnyL9EMa20a31vU48bvliUxsUxvphRaW8vg5K_xutrY/mobilebasic\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, there's not much available to help converting slashers. You may be happy to hear that the planned second edition Hunter book features The Slasher Chronicle, so this stuff is in the works, but I wouldn't recommend holding your breath for it. Onyx Path always prioritizes quality over speedy release, so it could be a while before the Slasher Chronicle is out. In the mean time, there's always <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/129193/Hunter-Mortal-Remains\" target=\"_blank\">Mortal Remains</a>, a sourcebook for 1st edition Hunter with a chapter containing advice on conversion for second edition games. It's somewhat bare bones and mostly focuses on converting material from the Hunter the Vigil core book - certainly it won't be much help in converting Slashers. But it might at least get you started and give you some inspiration for your own homebrew conversion.<br /> <br /> Finally, the forums are a good resource for advice and homebrew. If you have specific things you'd like to convert, try asking around to see if anyone has already converted them for their home games and if they would be willing to share their experiences.<br /> <br /> Best of luck! I hope your group enjoys making the switch to second edition/CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T01:10:03-07:00","id":858822,"title":"","content":"I think we've got Mage, Changeling and Promethean to come out before we get to Hunter. So yeah, that'll be a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}